#
# SGLang v0.5.16 + our SM121 build patches. Next production line, NOT YET
# GPU-VALIDATED — production stays on sglang-0.5.15.post1-sm121.recipe until it
# is. Created 2026-07-28 to evaluate the v0.5.16 line (released 2026-07-25,
# 574 PRs / 169 contributors).
#
# ── RENAMED 2026-08-02: sglang-0.5.16-dev-sm121 → sglang-0.5.16-sm121 ───────
# Tag accordingly xomoxcc/dgx-spark-sglang:0.5.16-dev-sm121 → :0.5.16-sm121
# (same for xomoxcc/dgx-spark-quant, see build_dgx_spark_quant_image.sh).
# TWO reasons, the first is the load-bearing one:
#   1. The `-dev` tag on Docker Hub (both repos, pushed 2026-07-28) is a
#      DIFFERENT ARTEFACT: it carries flashinfer 0.6.16rc3. It is cited as the
#      measurement basis by p36_flashinfer_plan_uniform_q_len.py ("Image
#      0.5.16-dev-sm121, flashinfer 0.6.16rc3"), p37_nvfp4_kv_spec_native_
#      verify.py and model_profiles/vroomfondel-qwen3.6-35b-a3b-nvfp4-mtp-
#      modelopt.yml. Rebuilding the flashinfer-0.6.16-final image UNDER THE SAME
#      TAG would silently change what those findings point at — precisely the
#      mutable-tag trap of the cutlass-dsl 4.5.2 wheel-swap incident. New
#      content gets a new tag; the rc3 tag stays frozen as the reference for
#      those three files (do NOT retarget their comments).
#   2. `-dev` has never meant "unvalidated" in this repo, it marked SIDE lines
#      (0.5.13-dev-nemotronh-mtp, the retired *-dev1 pair). Every mainline
#      recipe (0.5.11 … 0.5.15.post1) carried no suffix and was likewise
#      unvalidated on the day it was written. v0.5.16 is the mainline successor,
#      not a side experiment.
#
# THE HEADLINE: this is the first ref where our CORE SM121 kernel patch is
# GONE, not merged. SGLang PR #30448 ("Refactor FP4 quantization and remove
# deprecated JIT kernels", 2026-07-14) DELETED
#   python/sglang/jit_kernel/csrc/moe/nvfp4_blockwise_moe.cuh
# together with cutlass_moe_fp4() in srt/layers/moe/cutlass_moe.py. That .cuh
# is the file sgl-kernel-sm121.patch has patched since the 0.5.10 line (the
# StageCount<1> / non-pingpong fix for the 101 KB SM121 shared-memory budget,
# CUTLASS_NVFP4_SM121_PRD.md). Upstream now dispatches NVFP4 MoE to
# FlashInfer-CUTLASS on SM100 AND SM120/121, which is exactly the backend our
# model profiles already pin (moe_runner_backend: flashinfer_cutlass), so the
# fix is not needed, it is unreachable. Hence APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_SM121=0 below,
# a new gate added to dockerfile-sm121.patch for this recipe.
#
# ── DELTA gegenüber sglang-0.5.15.post1-sm121.recipe ────────────────────────
#   1. SGLANG_VERSION 0.5.15.post1 → 0.5.16, SGLANG_REF → v0.5.16.
#   2. APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_SM121=0 (NEW KNOB, default 1 everywhere else). See
#      above. Its dry-run would abort the build on this ref.
#   3. TILELANG_PATCH_VARIANT="-v0.5.16" (NEW KNOB). RFC #29630 moved the DSA
#      tilelang kernel to python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/ AND upstream
#      adopted the 2D-shared-buffer half of our compat fix, so the canonical
#      patch neither finds its file nor applies. The variant carries only the
#      remaining uint8-view hunk at the new path.
#   4. FLASHINFER_VERSION 0.6.15.post1 → 0.6.16 (final, 2026-07-31). The SECOND
#      driver of this recipe, see the FLASHINFER_VERSION block below for the
#      GB10-specific content. Was pinned to 0.6.16rc3 from 2026-07-28 until
#      2026-08-02; the RC caveat is GONE, this is now a stable release.
#   5. CUTLASS_DSL / TRANSFORMERS / KERNELS: UNCHANGED pins (4.6.1 / 5.12.1 /
#      0.14.1). v0.5.16's own pyproject moved flashinfer 0.6.12 → 0.6.14 and
#      cutlass-dsl 4.5.2 → 4.6.0, i.e. upstream caught up to roughly where we
#      already were; our overrides stay ahead and stay necessary. transformers
#      (==5.12.1) and kernels (>=0.14.1,<0.15) are byte-identical to
#      v0.5.15.post1, so do NOT bump them (PyPI has transformers 5.14.1 /
#      kernels 0.16.0; both are irrelevant here, kernels 0.16 would even violate
#      the upstream constraint).
#      v0.5.16 also DROPPED the flashinfer_cubin pin from its own pyproject, but
#      the scitrera Dockerfile installs flashinfer-python + flashinfer-cubin +
#      flashinfer-jit-cache all at ${FLASHINFER_VERSION} from flashinfer.ai, so
#      cubin stays version-locked to our pin either way.
#   6. BASE_IMAGE unchanged (torch 2.12/cu132). v0.5.16 still pins torch==2.11.0
#      upstream, same relationship as before. NO pytorch-base rebuild needed.
#   7. New transitive deps pulled by v0.5.16: helion==0.2.6,
#      humming-kernels[cu13]==0.1.10, numba==0.65.1, quack-kernels>=0.6.1,
#      llguidance>=1.7.6 (was 0.7.x), sgl-deep-gemm 0.1.4.post1, sglang-kernel
#      0.4.5, tokenspeed_mla 0.1.8, flash-attn-4>=4.0.0b18. All of these publish
#      aarch64 or py3-none-any wheels (checked on PyPI 2026-07-28), so none is a
#      known arm64 build blocker. AUDIO_DEPS still installs librosa, which now
#      overlaps with the upstream numba pin.
#
# ── PATCH VERIFY (2026-07-28, non-GPU, dry-run vs raw v0.5.16 source) ───────
#   ✅ sgl-kernel-arch-prune.patch              hunks at 124/206 (offset -12/-11)
#   ✅ sgl-kernel-disable-fa3-mainahead.patch   clean
#   ✅ sgl-kernel-skip-sm90-target-mainahead.patch  hunks at 319/338/370 (-4)
#   ✅ sgl-kernel-skip-flashmla.patch           hunk at 550 (offset +36)
#   ✅ sglang-dsv4-mtp-marlin-v0.5.14.patch     hunk at 1369 (offset -77)
#   ✅ sglang-tilelang-018-indexer-compat-v0.5.16.patch  clean (new variant)
#   ❌ sgl-kernel-sm121.patch                   target file deleted → GATED OFF
#   sgl-kernel/CMakeLists.txt survived the namespace migration, so all four
#   CMake patches keep working; SGL_KERNEL_MAINAHEAD stays 1 (the mscclpp link
#   refactor is still in the tree).
#
# ── OPEN RISKS, validate before this recipe is promoted ──────────────────────
#   A. moe_runner_backend cutlass / triton for NVFP4 is GONE with #30448. Two
#      model profiles opt out of flashinfer_cutlass and must be re-tested or
#      re-pinned: nvidia/Qwen3.5-397B-A17B-NVFP4 (cutlass) and Minimax-M2.5 at
#      PP=4 (triton). See TURBOQUANT.md for why they diverged.
#   B. compressed-tensors NVFP4 MoE with apply_router_weight_on_input=True now
#      ASSERTS instead of running (also #30448).
#   C. RUNTIME patches (roles/k8s_dgx/files/sglang_patches/) — MEASURED on the
#      BUILT image, 2026-07-28 (spark5 podman, all 39 patches run exactly as
#      sglang_launch.sh runs them, three env scenarios: bare / GLM-5.2+
#      SGLANG_DSA_INDEXER_TRITON / Hy3. Same battery against
#      0.5.15.post1-sm121 as the control: 0 drift there, so every hit below is
#      caused by the version bump, not pre-existing rot).
#      33 of 39 apply cleanly. SIX drift (identical in all three scenarios):
#        p24_linear_nvfp4_scale        linear.py: anchor gone. `weight_scale_2`
#                                      and `nvfp4` no longer appear in linear.py
#                                      at all, so this is a RE-TARGET, not an
#                                      anchor bump. Check first whether upstream
#                                      PR #29151 landed and the patch is dead.
#        p26_cutlass_moe_zeroinit      cutlass_moe.py: a_map/c_map/topk_weights
#                                      still there but `cutlass_moe_fp4` is GONE
#                                      (#30448). The zero-init fix was for the
#                                      FP4 path → likely simply OBSOLETE; the
#                                      fp8 path (cutlass_fused_experts_fp8) is
#                                      untouched by this patch.
#        p28_modelopt_cutlass_params_ep  modelopt_quant.py: the whole
#                                      `CutlassMoEParams` class is gone → the EP
#                                      fix has no target any more. Verify where
#                                      EP expert counts are computed now.
#        p31_dsa_flashinfer_gather     server_args.py + dsa_backend.py: both
#                                      files and DSA_CHOICES still exist, only
#                                      the surrounding code moved → ANCHOR
#                                      REBASE. (p31-p33 are the FALLBACK gather
#                                      path, not the live-proven one.)
#        p33_dsa_fig_graph_split       dsa_backend.py S1-init-state: same,
#                                      anchor rebase.
#        p34_dsa_trtllm_sparse_sm120   model_runner_kv_cache_mixin.py is GONE;
#                                      its content now lives in
#                                      srt/model_executor/pool_configurator.py
#                                      (get_num_kv_heads / kv_lora_rank there).
#                                      Second hunk (forward_mla.py fuse-rope off
#                                      on SM12x) needs an anchor rebase.
#                                      THIS ONE MATTERS: p34 is the live-proven
#                                      GLM-5.2 DSA path
#                                      (reference_glm52_dsa_indexer_deepgemm_sm121).
#      CORRECTION to the earlier static analysis: p30 and p35 are FINE. Their
#      "missing" targets (torch_paged_mqa_logits.py, triton_paged_mqa_logits.py)
#      are files these patches CREATE, not files they edit — both report
#      "created" on the built image.
#      Drift is logged as a warning and never crashes the pod, so a deploy would
#      SILENTLY run without those six fixes. GLM-5.2 must not be served off this
#      image before p34 is re-pathed.
#      ✅ RESOLVED 2026-08-02 — acceptance gate CLEAN on the 0.6.16-final image
#         (scripts/verify_sglang_image.sh xomoxcc/dgx-spark-sglang:0.5.16-sm121
#         spark5, image id e13762c84ff9):
#           bare / glm / hy3 — each: 0 ANCHOR-DRIFT, model registry no regression
#           baseline 2 pre-existing upstream failures (bailing_moe_linear,
#           bailing_moe_nextn — optional vllm dep, excluded by design)
#         All six were fixed between 2026-07-28 and 2026-08-02, in two DIFFERENT
#         ways — the distinction matters, "0 drift" alone does not mean "the fix
#         still runs":
#           RE-TARGETED (patch still applies, fix is live):
#             p24 f17cfda  markers switched to upstream anchor strings
#             p34 d21f59e  made v0.5.16-compatible — THE one that mattered, the
#                          live-proven GLM-5.2 DSA path is fixed, so the "do not
#                          serve GLM-5.2 off this image" block above is LIFTED
#           SELF-GATED OFF on >= 0.5.16 (patch deliberately no-ops, fix is gone
#           because its target is gone — silent by design, not a regression):
#             p26 80c6cc3  gated on cutlass_moe_fp4 being present (#30448 removed it)
#             p28 fd8a937  made conditional on the anchor existing
#             p31 2d0c0e3  gated to pre-0.5.16 (fallback gather path)
#             p33          same gate as p31 (p31-p33 are one fallback path)
#         So the gate being green is NOT the same as all six fixes being active.
#         Four of them are intentionally inert here. Re-read risks A and B before
#         serving the affected NVFP4 profiles.
#      ⚠️ SCOPE: the gate is IMPORT-level (does a patch still find its anchor,
#         does the model registry still import). It executes no kernel and serves
#         no token. Risks A, B, E and G stay open until a real serving run.
#      Possible upside to check while re-porting: v0.5.16 ships a vectorized,
#      CUDA-graph-safe fp8_paged_mqa_logits_torch_sm120 in
#      srt/layers/attention/dsv4/indexer.py (present in the image, verified),
#      i.e. upstream may have absorbed what p30 does by hand.
#   D. Flag renames in v0.5.16: --enable-deepep-waterfill → --enable-waterfill,
#      --optimistic-prefill-retries → --optimistic-prefill-attempts. Grep the
#      model profiles and sglang_launch.sh before serving.
#      SEPARATE, PRE-EXISTING ISSUE — deprecated flags. NOT a v0.5.16 delta:
#      Loki shows the identical warnings from PRODUCTION pods on the
#      0.5.15.post1 image (and some already on 0.5.15), so this backlog predates
#      the bump and does not block it. Query used:
#        {namespace="sglang"} |= "is deprecated and will be removed in a future release"
#      Four flags, all emitted by sglang_launch.sh / profile keys:
#        --cuda-graph-max-bs            → --cuda-graph-max-bs-decode       (last 07-16)
#        --disable-cuda-graph           → --cuda-graph-backend-{decode,prefill}=disabled
#                                                                          (last 07-16)
#        --disable-piecewise-cuda-graph → --cuda-graph-backend-prefill=disabled
#                                                                          (last 07-25)
#        --mamba-scheduler-strategy     → --mamba-radix-cache-strategy     (last 07-25)
#      ✅ FIXED 2026-07-28 in sglang_launch.sh: it now emits the new spellings
#      unconditionally. No version probe needed — BOTH spellings exist in
#      0.5.15.post1 AND 0.5.16 (checked against `--help` in both images), and a
#      start with the new flags produces neither "unrecognized arguments" nor a
#      deprecation warning on either. Note that two of them are not plain
#      renames: --disable-cuda-graph maps to BOTH
#      --cuda-graph-backend-{decode,prefill} disabled, and the piecewise branch is
#      suppressed when the full-disable branch already turned prefill off.
#      Profile keys are unchanged (cuda_graph_max_bs, disable_cuda_graph,
#      disable_piecewise_cuda_graph, mamba_scheduler_strategy) — this is purely a
#      launch-script concern.
#   E. UnifiedRadixTree is now the DEFAULT for SWA / Mamba / DSA models, and
#      QServe + FBGEMM FP8 quantization were removed. Behaviour change, not a
#      build break.
#   F. flashinfer is two minor steps over SGLang's own 0.6.14 pin. Rollback
#      order in the FLASHINFER_VERSION block.
#      ✅ RC RISK RETIRED 2026-08-02: 0.6.16 went final on 2026-07-31, the pin
#         moved rc3 → 0.6.16. 21 commits rc3..final, all fixes/cherry-picks
#         (details in the FLASHINFER_VERSION block), no SM121 feature churn.
#      ✅ CLEARED 2026-07-28 on GB10 (spark5, podman --device nvidia.com/gpu=all):
#         rmsnorm smoke test PASSES on the built image (no mlir_global_dtors ICE,
#         output finite, max abs err 0.0144 vs fp32 reference = bf16 rounding).
#         cutlass-dsl 4.6.1 + flashinfer 0.6.16rc3 is therefore a working pair.
#      ✅ RE-CLEARED 2026-08-02 on the 0.6.16-FINAL build (image id e13762c84ff9,
#         spark5 idle: k3s inactive, no containers, no GPU processes). The rerun
#         was NOT optional: #4226 (rc4) made the CuTe-DSL arch guard env-aware and
#         gates norm's DSL dispatch on it, i.e. it rewrote exactly this path.
#           rmsnorm(4x512 bf16): shape (4,512), finite True,
#           max abs err 0.014897 vs fp32 reference — same bf16-rounding regime as
#           the rc3 run (0.0144), no ICE.
#         AND the dispatch was verified to actually TAKE the DSL path, so the
#         green result is not a silent CUDA-JIT fallback masking the ICE:
#           _cute_dsl_supports_arch(12,1) = True
#           is_cute_dsl_arch_supported(12,1) = True
#           norm._use_cuda_norm(cuda:0) = False   ← False means DSL, not CUDA JIT
#           the *_cute symbols (rmsnorm_cute, fused_add_rmsnorm_cute, …) all
#           imported, i.e. cutlass-dsl 4.6.1 is accepted as compatible
#         Re-check these four on any flashinfer or cutlass-dsl bump: norm/__init__
#         .py falls back to CUDA JIT SILENTLY when the DSL cannot target the arch
#         (or CUTE_DSL_ARCH is unset for a new one), and then the smoke test goes
#         green without ever compiling a DSL kernel.
#      ℹ️  The cudnn-frontend>=1.25 concern is MOOT: nvidia-cudnn-frontend is not
#         installed in this image AT ALL, and it is equally absent from the live
#         0.5.15.post1-sm121 image. Status quo, not a regression. Only matters if
#         something ever routes onto a flashinfer cudnn backend.
#   G. NVFP4 attention is NEW on SM121 with flashinfer #3897, it never ran on
#      this hardware before.
#      ✅ KERNEL-LEVEL VERIFIED 2026-07-28 on GB10 (spark5):
#         is_sm121a_supported() = True, and
#         nvfp4_attention_sm120_quantize_qkv + _fwd run end to end at
#         [1, 8, 512, 128] bf16 causal: output finite, cosine 0.9909 and rel-L2
#         0.135 vs an fp32 SDPA reference (the expected 4-bit loss profile), and
#         2.65x faster than torch SDPA bf16 on the fwd (indicative single-shape
#         timing, upstream claims 2.3-2.4x vs FA2 at head_dim 128).
#      ⏳ STILL OPEN: end-to-end through SGLang with a real uniform-NVFP4 model
#         (attention included). Judge output quality by pattern-grep + token
#         distribution + tail, not by finish_reason. The companion correctness
#         fix #3838 (SM120 NVFP4 qk_correction / row-sum / lse) makes this the
#         natural moment to re-test the still-open Hy3/HYV3 W4A4 NaN as well.
#
# Voraussetzungen: xomoxcc/dgx-spark-pytorch-dev:2.12.0-v1-cu132 Base auf dem
# Build-Host (scripts/build_pytorch_base_image.sh, siehe
# ensure_base_image_present in build_sm121_image.sh).
#
DOCKERFILE=Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
TARGET=runtime

BASE_IMAGE=xomoxcc/dgx-spark-pytorch-dev:2.12.0-v1-cu132

# Override über den v0.5.16-Upstream-Pin (flashinfer_python[cu13]==0.6.14) hinaus
# auf 0.6.16 FINAL (2026-07-31, 134 Commits über 0.6.15.post1). Bewusst gewählt,
# weil in diesem Fenster ungewöhnlich viel GB10-spezifische Arbeit gelandet ist.
# Mit SGLang PR #30448 hängt der NVFP4-MoE-Pfad auf SM120/121 ohnehin KOMPLETT an
# flashinfer (der eigene cutlass_moe_fp4-Pfad ist weg), der Pin wiegt also
# schwerer als je.
#
# Der Pin stand vom 2026-07-28 bis 2026-08-02 auf 0.6.16rc3 (dem damals einzigen
# 0.6.16-Prerelease). Damit ist die offene Frage "RC-Politik" aus
# FLASHINFER_0.6.16rc3_TODO.local.md §0 erledigt: wir bleiben bei der bisherigen
# Linie und pinnen nur Stables.
#
# Was 0.6.16 für SM121/GB10 bringt (Commit-Range v0.5.15.post1...v0.6.16):
#   • #3897 feat(attention): enable SM121 (GB10/DGX Spark) for NVFP4 attention.
#     DER Grund für diesen Bump. Der SM120-NVFP4-Attention-Kernel kompiliert und
#     läuft laut PR unverändert als sm_121a; es fehlten nur die
#     Capability-Checks / AOT- und JIT-Arch-Gates. Vorher war NVFP4-Attention auf
#     SM121 schlicht nicht verfügbar. Benchmark im PR: 2.3-2.4x gegenüber FA2-BF16
#     bei head_dim 128 (bei head_dim 64 nur noch 1.5-1.6x). Das ist genau der
#     Pfad, den der bevorzugte uniform-NVFP4-Quant-Weg (inkl. Attention) braucht.
#   • #3838 fix(attention): correct SM120 NVFP4 qk_correction layout, row-sum
#     reduction and lse. KORREKTHEITS-Fix im NVFP4-Attention-Pfad. Beim
#     Validieren gegen den offenen W4A4-NaN auf Hy3/HYV3 gegenprüfen: anderer
#     Kernel, aber dieselbe Familie.
#   • #3960 fix(gdn): compile SM12x CuteDSL kernels as sm_121a on DGX Spark.
#     Explizit DGX Spark, betrifft GDN/linear-attention (Qwen3.5MoE-Familie).
#   • #3655 feat(attn): MiniMax Sparse Attention (MSA) für Consumer-Blackwell
#     (SM120/121). #3016 fmha_v2 HMMA attention für SM120 standard shapes.
#   • #3891 FP8 groupwise MoE GEMM entry (cute SM120 backend), #3947 dead
#     SM12x-gencode aus SM10x-Modulen entfernt (kleinere JIT-Last).
#   • #3922 fix(cute_dsl): migrate off APIs removed in nvidia-cutlass-dsl 4.6
#     (behält 4.5.x-Kompatibilität). Macht die Paarung mit unserem 4.6.1-Pin
#     unten EXPLIZIT unterstützt — 0.6.15 ist älter als diese API-Entfernung.
#   • Viel MoE-Arbeit ohne direkten SM121-Bezug (MegaMoE, unified MoE API,
#     NVFP4-Finalize, mm_fp4-Autotune-Cache).
#
# Was rc3 → 0.6.16 final noch dazukam (21 Commits, rc4 + rc5 + final; geprüft
# 2026-08-02 via GitHub compare v0.6.16rc3...v0.6.16). Ausschließlich Fixes und
# Cherry-Picks, KEINE neue SM121-Funktionalität — die vier mit Relevanz hier:
#   • #4226 "Make CuTe-DSL arch guard env-aware and gate norm's DSL dispatch on
#     it" (rc4). Berührt genau den rmsnorm-CuTe-Pfad, den unser GB10-Smoke-Test
#     abdeckt → Smoke-Test auf dem final-Build WIEDERHOLEN (Risiko F oben).
#   • #4213 + #4235 fix(moe): inkompatible output-scale-Cubins ablehnen bzw. per
#     Name filtern, bis die gepinnten Pakete mDtypeSfC tragen. NVFP4-MoE-Pfad,
#     also unser Hauptpfad seit SGLang #30448.
#   • #4230 fix(trtllm): routed-MoE-Backends auf unterstützte Architekturen
#     beschränken (Release-Port von #4107).
#   • #4288 fix(moe): trtllm-gen route map um ein Element padden (OOB-Read).
#
# WAS ZU PRÜFEN IST:
#   • Der Dockerfile-Schritt installiert aus dem flashinfer-eigenen Index. Alle
#     DREI Pakete existieren dort in 0.6.16 final, inklusive des aarch64/cu130-
#     Rades (geprüft 2026-08-02 gegen https://flashinfer.ai/whl):
#       flashinfer-python  0.6.16  (py3-none-any)
#       flashinfer-cubin   0.6.16  (py3-none-any)   ← NICHT auf PyPI, nur hier
#       flashinfer-jit-cache 0.6.16+cu130 manylinux_2_28_aarch64 (1.71 GB;
#         rc3 war 1.70 GB. Die frühere "1.6 GB / kleiner als 0.6.15.post1"-Notiz
#         war falsch, das gencode-Pruning aus #3947 schlägt nicht auf die
#         Wheel-Größe durch.)
#     `uv pip install --pre` bleibt im Dockerfile harmlos, wird für einen Stable
#     aber nicht mehr gebraucht.
#   • flashinfer 0.6.16 verlangt nvidia-cudnn-frontend>=1.25.0 (0.6.15: >=1.13.0).
#     Der Dockerfile installiert flashinfer mit --no-deps, die Anforderung wird
#     also NICHT automatisch erfüllt. Auf dem gebauten Image gegenprüfen:
#       python3 -c "import importlib.metadata as m; print(m.version('nvidia-cudnn-frontend'))"
#     Falls < 1.25: entweder nachinstallieren oder auf 0.6.15.post1 zurück.
#     (Risiko F oben: aktuell MOOT, das Paket ist im Image gar nicht installiert.)
#   • Wir liegen mit diesem Pin ZWEI Minor-Schritte über SGLangs eigenem
#     0.6.14-Pin. Bei jedem unerklärlichen Kernel-Fehler ist dieser Pin der erste
#     Rollback-Kandidat.
# Roll-back-Reihenfolge: 0.6.15.post1 (live-validiert auf 0.5.15.post1-sm121),
# dann 0.6.14 (= Upstream-Pin von v0.5.16). 0.6.16rc3 nur als Referenz für den
# GB10-Smoke-Test vom 2026-07-28, NICHT als Rollback-Ziel (Stable-only-Politik).
# FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.14
# FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.15.post1
# FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.16rc3
FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.16

# transformers 5.12.1 — exakt v0.5.16s pyproject-Pin (==5.12.1, unverändert ggü.
# v0.5.15/post1). NICHT isoliert über die SGLang-Ref hinaus bumpen (kein
# Perf-Nutzen, transformers ist nicht im Inferenz-Hot-Path; PyPI-latest 5.14.1
# ist irrelevant).
TRANSFORMERS_VERSION=5.12.1

# kernels 0.14.1 — exakt v0.5.16s pyproject-Constraint (kernels>=0.14.1,<0.15,
# unverändert). PyPI-latest 0.16.0 verletzt das Constraint. PERF-NEUTRAL für
# SM121: der einzige hub-geladene Kernel (sgl-flash-attn3) ist auf GB10 hart
# deaktiviert und hat keine sm_121/ARM64-Builds.
KERNELS_VERSION=0.14.1

# nvidia-cutlass-dsl 4.6.1 — explicit pin, force-reinstalled late in the build.
# v0.5.16 pinnt upstream 4.6.0; flashinfer 0.6.16 verlangt weiterhin nur
# >=4.5.0 (open-ended, unverändert seit 0.6.14, und identisch in rc3 und final
# — die Dependency-Metadaten der beiden sind byte-gleich), und NVIDIA hat schon einmal
# unterschiedlichen Wheel-Inhalt unter derselben Versionsnummer ausgeliefert
# (4.5.2-Vorfall, mlir_global_dtors-'data' ICE, reference_cutlass_dsl_wheel_swap)
# — der explizite Pin bleibt Pflicht.
# NEU mit 0.6.16: PR #3922 migriert flashinfer weg von den in cutlass-dsl 4.6
# entfernten APIs (bei erhaltener 4.5.x-Kompatibilität). Die Paarung 4.6.1 +
# flashinfer ist damit erstmals explizit upstream-unterstützt statt nur
# empirisch getestet — ein Argument FÜR den 0.6.16-Bump, nicht dagegen.
# ⚠️  MUST GPU-verify auf dem gebauten Image vor Deploy (rmsnorm smoke test):
#   python -c "import flashinfer, torch; \
#     from flashinfer.norm import rmsnorm; \
#     x=torch.randn(4,512,device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16); \
#     w=torch.randn(512,device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16); \
#     print(rmsnorm(x,w).shape)"
# Fallback: 4.6.0 (jetzt der Upstream-Pin), dann 4.5.1 (letztes pre-swap release).
# CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION=4.6.0
CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION=4.6.1

# Audio multimodal deps — siehe 0.5.15.post1-Recipe. v0.5.16 zieht numba jetzt
# selbst (numba==0.65.1), librosa bleibt trotzdem nötig (soundfile/audioread).
AUDIO_DEPS="librosa"

# accelerate — baked into the image (ModelOptModelLoader importiert es).
ACCELERATE_DEPS="accelerate"

SGLANG_VERSION=0.5.16
SGLANG_REF="v0.5.16"

# main-ahead sgl-kernel patch variant. Der mscclpp-Link-Refactor ist in v0.5.16
# weiterhin präsent, also bleibt SGL_KERNEL_MAINAHEAD=1 (installiert die
# "-mainahead"-Geschwister für skip-sm90-target + disable-fa3 unter dem
# kanonischen Namen). Alle vier CMakeLists-Patches wurden gegen v0.5.16
# dry-run-verifiziert (siehe PATCH VERIFY oben).
SGL_KERNEL_MAINAHEAD=1

# ── CORE SM121 JIT-Header-Patch: TARGET WEG (PR #30448) → OFF ────────────────
# python/sglang/jit_kernel/csrc/moe/nvfp4_blockwise_moe.cuh existiert in v0.5.16
# nicht mehr; cutlass_moe_fp4() ist ebenfalls raus. NVFP4-MoE läuft auf
# SM100/SM120/SM121 jetzt über FlashInfer-CUTLASS, also über den Backend, den
# unsere Profile ohnehin pinnen. Bei 1 würde der in-container dry-run den Build
# abbrechen. Gate lebt in dockerfile-sm121.patch (ARG APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_SM121,
# default 1 → alle älteren Recipes bleiben unverändert).
# Konsequenz für die Profile: siehe OPEN RISK A oben.
APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_SM121=0

# ── DeepSeek-V4 FlashMLA kernel: DROPPED (nativ seit v0.5.13) ────────────────
FLASH_MLA_REPO=
FLASH_MLA_REF=
DSV4_KERNEL_REPO=
DSV4_KERNEL_REF=
DSV4_KERNEL_ARCH=

# ── DeepSeek-V4 NVFP4 MoE: NATIV seit v0.5.14 (PR #25820) → OFF ─────────────
APPLY_DSV4_NVFP4_PR25820=0

# ── DeepSeek-V4 EAGLE-MTP marlin branch + TileLang-Indexer-Compat → ON ───────
# Unveränderte Begründung ggü. 0.5.15.post1: HybridFp8NvFp4Config.get_quant_method
# hat weiterhin keinen marlin-Zweig für die MTP/nextn-Draft-MoE-Layer, und der
# TileLang-uint8-Arg-Check greift weiterhin. Beide Source-Patches am 2026-07-28
# gegen v0.5.16 dry-run-verifiziert (marlin: Hunk bei 1369, offset -77; tilelang:
# neue Variante, clean). Der tilelang-Patch kommt hier aus der v0.5.16-Variante,
# siehe TILELANG_PATCH_VARIANT unten.
APPLY_DSV4_MTP_MARLIN_TILELANG=1

# Variante des tilelang-Compat-Patches. Leer/fehlend = kanonische Datei
# (sglang-tilelang-018-indexer-compat.patch, Pfad srt/layers/attention/dsa/).
# "-v0.5.16" wählt sglang-tilelang-018-indexer-compat-v0.5.16.patch: neuer Pfad
# (kernels/ops/attention/dsa/) und nur noch der uint8-View-Hunk, weil upstream
# den 2D-alloc_shared-Fix übernommen hat. apply_patches() installiert die
# gewählte Datei unter dem kanonischen Namen in den Build-Context, der
# Dockerfile-Schritt bleibt also unverändert.
TILELANG_PATCH_VARIANT="-v0.5.16"

# ── Qwen3.6 ModelOpt mixed NVFP4: MERGED (PR #27906) → OFF ───────────────────
# ⚠️  Der OPEN dispatch fix #28099 ist ein RUNTIME-Patch in sglang_launch.sh und
#     von diesem Flag unberührt (p21/p22) — Qwen3.6 live gegenprüfen.
APPLY_QWEN36_MIXED_NVFP4_PR27906=0

IMAGE_TAG=xomoxcc/dgx-spark-sglang:0.5.16-sm121
